  "query_preview": "..\nA cold front associated with an upper-level trough digging over\neastern Montana will be well to our southeast Thursday morning. \nNW winds in its wake will continue through Thursday, diminishing \nby Thursday evening. A Lake Wind Advisory is in effect through \nThursday. \n\nThe trough will rapidly exit eastward Thursday evening ahead of a\nstrong upper-level ridge building over the western United States.\nThe ridging pattern will produce warm and dry conditions Friday \nand Saturday.\n\nThe ridge will gradually translate eastward ahead of an\napproaching upper-level trough over the weekend. Minor \nperturbations embedded within the resultant SW flow aloft may \nelevate winds slightly early in the weekend, but no significant \ndeviations from the ridge-induced weather regime are expected.\n\nThe aforementioned trough is expected to weaken before digging \nover Montana by Sunday morning, resulting in a dry frontal passage\nSaturday night and daily high temperatures in the low-to-mid 60s\nthroughout the first half of next week.\n\nFlow aloft over the central United States will back SW over the\ncourse of Monday as an Aleutian low digs southward, settling off\nthe coast of central California by Tuesday morning. Current model\nguidance indicates the atmosphere will be relatively dry during \nthis period. Little change to the perceptible weather is \nanticipated.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\n- There is high confidence in conditions remaining largely benign\n  throughout the forecast period.\n\n- No deviations from the NBM. TFJ",
